A table renamed in schema.sql and nothing more is, to SQLite's listings,
one table gone and another new: refused, since the old one's rows would
go. One table is new, so the error writes the rename step with both names.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `dish` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its rows would go. Renamed? Add the step to ledger.sql: `ALTER TABLE dish RENAME TO meal;` Gone on purpose? `DROP TABLE dish;`
